      "steps": [
        {
          "key": "open-create",
          "title": "Open the flexible server create wizard",
          "instruction": "In the portal menu, select **Azure Database for PostgreSQL**, then select **Create**.",
          "hint": "The create command is in the flexible server list command bar.",
          "explanation": "Azure Database for PostgreSQL flexible server is the Azure managed service for open-source PostgreSQL workloads.",
          "targetId": "pg-create",
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "visited-create",
              "description": "You opened the create wizard",
              "rule": {
                "type": "visited",
                "page": "pg-create"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "basics",
          "title": "Configure Basics",
          "instruction": "Create resource group **rg-open-source-data**, set **Server name** to **pg-flex-orders-01**, choose **(Europe) West Europe**, **PostgreSQL version** **16**, and **Workload type** **Development**.",
          "hint": "Server names become part of the host name, so use lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens.",
          "explanation": "Basics identify where the managed server lives and which PostgreSQL engine version it runs.",
          "targetId": "pg-wizard",
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "rg-created",
              "description": "Resource group exists",
              "rule": {
                "type": "arrayContains",
                "path": "resourceGroups",
                "match": {
                  "name": "rg-open-source-data",
                  "location": "westeurope"
                }
              },
              "failureFeedback": "Create rg-open-source-data in West Europe."
            },
            {
              "key": "server-basics",
              "description": "The server uses the required name, version and workload type",
              "rule": {
                "type": "arrayContains",
                "path": "postgresServers",
                "match": {
                  "name": "pg-flex-orders-01",
                  "location": "westeurope",
                  "postgresVersion": "16",
                  "workloadType": "Development"
                }
              },
              "failureFeedback": "Check server name, region, version and workload type."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "compute-auth",
          "title": "Choose compute, storage and authentication",
          "instruction": "On **Compute + storage**, use **Burstable**, **Small training profile**, and **Training storage profile**. On **Authentication**, choose **Microsoft Entra authentication only** and set **Microsoft Entra admin** to **Data Platform Team (data-platform@contoso.example)**.",
          "hint": "Do not choose PostgreSQL authentication only; this lab avoids database passwords.",
          "explanation": "Compute and storage size the managed service; Microsoft Entra authentication lets organizations use centralized identity instead of shared database passwords.",
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "compute-choice",
              "description": "Training compute and storage profile selected",
              "rule": {
                "type": "arrayContains",
                "path": "postgresServers",
                "match": {
                  "name": "pg-flex-orders-01",
                  "computeTier": "Burstable",
                  "computeSize": "Small training profile",
                  "storageSize": "Training storage profile"
                }
              },
              "failureFeedback": "Use the requested training compute and storage choices."
            },
            {
              "key": "secure-auth",
              "description": "Server uses Microsoft Entra-based authentication",
              "rule": {
                "type": "arrayContains",
                "path": "postgresServers",
                "match": {
                  "name": "pg-flex-orders-01",
                  "authentication": "Microsoft Entra authentication only",
                  "entraAdmin": "Data Platform Team"
                }
              },
              "failureFeedback": "Use Microsoft Entra authentication only with the Data Platform Team admin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "networking",
          "title": "Limit public access to the lab client IP",
          "instruction": "On **Networking**, keep **Public access (allowed IP addresses)**, choose **Add current client IP address**, and keep both IP boxes as **203.0.113.24**. Do not choose **Allow all IPv4 addresses**. Select **Review + create** and **Create**.",
          "hint": "A public endpoint can still be restricted to a specific client IP. Opening 0.0.0.0 through 255.255.255.255 is rejected.",
          "explanation": "Firewall rules should permit only the client that needs access. Private access is also valid in real designs when clients are inside a virtual network.",
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "safe-firewall",
              "description": "Public firewall is limited to the current client IP",
              "rule": {
                "type": "arrayContains",
                "path": "postgresServers",
                "match": {
                  "name": "pg-flex-orders-01",
                  "networking": "Public access (allowed IP addresses)",
                  "firewallRule": "Add current client IP address",
                  "firewallStart": "203.0.113.24",
                  "firewallEnd": "203.0.113.24"
                }
              },
              "failureFeedback": "Limit the firewall to the current client IP, not all IPv4 addresses."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "connect-psql",
          "title": "Connect from Cloud Shell with psql",
          "instruction": "When deployment completes, select **Go to resource**, then **Connect**. In **Cloud Shell**, run `psql \"host=pg-flex-orders-01.postgres.database.azure.com port=5432 dbname=postgres user=alex@contoso.example sslmode=require\"`.",
          "hint": "Copy the full connection string, including `sslmode=require`.",
          "explanation": "psql is the standard PostgreSQL command-line client. Managed PostgreSQL still uses familiar open-source tools.",
          "targetId": "cloudshell",
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "psql-connected",
              "description": "The psql connection command was used",
              "rule": {
                "type": "commandUsed",
                "pattern": "^psql \"host=pg-flex-orders-01\\.postgres\\.database\\.azure\\.com port=5432 dbname=postgres user=alex@contoso\\.example sslmode=require\"$"
              },
              "failureFeedback": "Run the exact psql command from Cloud Shell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "create-insert",
          "title": "Create a table and insert rows",
          "instruction": "In **PostgreSQL query worksheet**, run `CREATE TABLE order_sales (order_id INT PRIMARY KEY, region VARCHAR(30), amount INT);`, then run `INSERT INTO order_sales(order_id, region, amount) VALUES (1, 'North', 120), (2, 'South', 95), (3, 'North', 80), (4, 'West', 140);`.",
          "hint": "The SQL is portable: a table definition followed by inserted rows.",
          "explanation": "CREATE TABLE defines a relational schema. INSERT adds rows that can be filtered and aggregated with SQL.",
          "targetId": "pg-query-editor",
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "table-created",
              "description": "order_sales table exists",
              "rule": {
                "type": "exists",
                "path": "sql.pgdb.tables.order_sales.columns.0.name"
              },
              "failureFeedback": "Run the CREATE TABLE statement."
            },
            {
              "key": "rows-inserted",
              "description": "Four order rows were inserted",
              "rule": {
                "type": "arrayLength",
                "path": "sql.pgdb.tables.order_sales.rows",
                "min": 4
              },
              "failureFeedback": "Run the INSERT statement with four rows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "group-query",
          "title": "Aggregate sales by region",
          "instruction": "Run `SELECT region, SUM(amount) AS total_amount FROM order_sales GROUP BY region ORDER BY total_amount DESC;`.",
          "hint": "GROUP BY produces one output row per region.",
          "explanation": "Relational databases use SQL aggregates to answer business questions such as totals by region without duplicating summary data.",
          "targetId": "pg-query-editor",
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "group-query-used",
              "description": "A GROUP BY aggregate query was run",
              "rule": {
                "type": "commandUsed",
                "pattern": "SELECT region, SUM\\(amount\\) AS total_amount FROM order_sales GROUP BY region ORDER BY total_amount DESC;?"
              },
              "failureFeedback": "Run the regional aggregate query exactly as written."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "finalRules": [
        {
          "key": "no-allow-all",
          "description": "Firewall is not open to all IPv4 addresses",
          "rule": {
            "type": "arrayNotContains",
            "path": "postgresServers",
            "match": {
              "name": "pg-flex-orders-01",
              "firewallRule": "Allow all IPv4 addresses"
            }
          },
          "successFeedback": "The firewall is limited to the lab client IP.",
          "failureFeedback": "Do not use an allow-all IPv4 firewall rule."
        },
        {
          "key": "not-password-only",
          "description": "Authentication is not PostgreSQL-only",
          "rule": {
            "type": "arrayNotContains",
            "path": "postgresServers",
            "match": {
              "name": "pg-flex-orders-01",
              "authentication": "PostgreSQL authentication only"
            }
          },
          "successFeedback": "Microsoft Entra-based authentication is used.",
          "failureFeedback": "Use Microsoft Entra authentication only or Microsoft Entra and PostgreSQL authentication."
        }
      ],
      "solution": "1. Select **Azure Database for PostgreSQL**, then **Create**.\n2. **Basics**: Resource group **Create new** -> `rg-open-source-data`; Server name `pg-flex-orders-01`; Region **(Europe) West Europe**; PostgreSQL version **16**; Workload type **Development**.\n3. **Compute + storage**: **Burstable**, **Small training profile**, **Training storage profile**.\n4. **Authentication**: **Microsoft Entra authentication only**; Microsoft Entra admin **Data Platform Team (data-platform@contoso.example)**.\n5. **Networking**: **Public access (allowed IP addresses)**, **Add current client IP address**, IP range `203.0.113.24` to `203.0.113.24`; then **Review + create** -> **Create**.\n6. **Go to resource** -> **Connect**. In **Cloud Shell**, run `psql \"host=pg-flex-orders-01.postgres.database.azure.com port=5432 dbname=postgres user=alex@contoso.example sslmode=require\"`.\n7. Run `CREATE TABLE order_sales (order_id INT PRIMARY KEY, region VARCHAR(30), amount INT);` and `INSERT INTO order_sales(order_id, region, amount) VALUES (1, 'North', 120), (2, 'South', 95), (3, 'North', 80), (4, 'West', 140);`.\n8. Run `SELECT region, SUM(amount) AS total_amount FROM order_sales GROUP BY region ORDER BY total_amount DESC;`."
    }
  ]
